# Line-wise Ex commands with ranges, typed from normal mode (change.txt, various.txt).

=== :d x deletes into a register
ref:    change.txt *:d*
quote:  Delete [range] lines (default: current line) [into register x].
given:
  one
  |two
  three
keys:   :d a<CR>
expect:
  one
  |three
regs:   "a = "two\n"   "" = "two\n"   "1 = "two\n"
mode:   normal

=== :d x with a count
ref:    change.txt *:d*
quote:  Delete {count} lines, starting with [range]
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2d b 2<CR>
expect:
  one
  |four
regs:   "b = "two\nthree\n"
mode:   normal

=== :d A appends to a register
ref:    change.txt *:d*
quote:  Delete [range] lines (default: current line) [into register x].
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :1d a<CR>:1d A<CR>
expect: |three
regs:   "a = "one\ntwo\n"
mode:   normal

=== :y yanks lines without moving the cursor
ref:    change.txt *:y*
quote:  Yank [range] lines [into register x].
given:
  one
  tw|o
  three
keys:   :1,2y<CR>
expect:
  one
  tw|o
  three
regs:   "" = "one\ntwo\n"   "0 = "one\ntwo\n"
mode:   normal

=== :y reports more than 'report' lines
ref:    options.txt *'report'*
quote:  When the number of changed lines is more than 'report' a message will be given for most ":" commands.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :%y<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
msg:    3 lines yanked
mode:   normal

=== :y x {count} starts at the last line of the range
ref:    change.txt *:y*
quote:  Yank {count} lines, starting with last line number in [range]
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :1,2y c 2<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
regs:   "c = "two\nthree\n"
mode:   normal

=== :m moves a line below an address
ref:    change.txt *:m*
quote:  Move the lines given by [range] to below the line given by {address}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :m3<CR>
expect:
  two
  three
  |one
  four
mode:   normal

=== :m0 moves a line to the top
ref:    change.txt *:m*
quote:  Move the lines given by [range] to below the line given by {address}.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
keys:   :m0<CR>
expect:
  |three
  one
  two
mode:   normal

=== :m-2 moves a line up one
ref:    change.txt *:m*
quote:  Move the lines given by [range] to below the line given by {address}.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
keys:   :m-2<CR>
expect:
  one
  |three
  two
mode:   normal

=== :m with a range reports moved lines
ref:    options.txt *'report'*
quote:  When the number of changed lines is more than 'report' a message will be given for most ":" commands.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :1,3m$<CR>
expect:
  four
  one
  two
  |three
msg:    3 lines moved
mode:   normal

=== :m into its own range is an error
ref:    change.txt *E134*
quote:  Move the lines given by [range] to below the line given by {address}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :1,2m1<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
msg:    "E134: Cannot move a range of lines into itself"
mode:   normal

=== :t copies a line below an address
ref:    change.txt *:t*
quote:  Synonym for copy.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :t$<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |one
mode:   normal

=== :co with a range copies to the top
ref:    change.txt *:co*
quote:  Copy the lines given by [range] to below the line given by {address}.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
keys:   :2,3co0<CR>
expect:
  two
  |three
  one
  two
  three
mode:   normal

=== :t. duplicates the cursor line
ref:    change.txt *:t*
quote:  Synonym for copy.
given:
  o|ne
  two
keys:   :t.<CR>
expect:
  one
  o|ne
  two
mode:   normal

=== :j joins with the next line
ref:    change.txt *:j*
quote:  The default behavior is to join the current line with the line below it.
given:
  |one
      two
  three
keys:   :j<CR>
expect:
  |one two
  three
mode:   normal

=== :j with a range joins every line in it
ref:    change.txt *:j*
quote:  Join [range] lines.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :1,3j<CR>
expect:
  |one two three
  four
mode:   normal

=== :j! keeps white space
ref:    change.txt *:j*
quote:  with [!] the join does not insert or delete any spaces.
given:
  |one
    two
keys:   :j!<CR>
expect: |one  two
mode:   normal

=== :j with a count
ref:    change.txt *:j*
quote:  Join {count} lines, starting with [range]
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2j 3<CR>
expect:
  one
  |two three four
mode:   normal

=== :j with equal start and end does nothing
ref:    change.txt *:j*
quote:  If a [range] has equal start and end values, this command does nothing.
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   :1,1j<CR>
expect:
  |one
  two
mode:   normal

=== :> shifts lines right
ref:    change.txt *:>*
quote:  Shift [range] lines one 'shiftwidth' right.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:1,2><CR>
expect:
    one
    |two
  three
mode:   normal

=== :>> shifts twice and reports
ref:    change.txt *:>*
quote:  Repeat '>' for shifting multiple 'shiftwidth's.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:%>><CR>
expect:
      one
      two
      |three
msg:    3 lines >ed 2 times
mode:   normal

=== :> with a count
ref:    change.txt *:>*
quote:  Shift {count} lines one 'shiftwidth' right, starting with [range]
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:> 2<CR>
expect:
    one
    |two
  three
mode:   normal

=== :< shifts lines left
ref:    change.txt *:<*
quote:  Shift [range] lines one 'shiftwidth' left.
given:
  |    one
      two
  three
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:%<<CR>
expect:
    one
    two
  th|ree
msg:    3 lines <ed 1 time
mode:   normal

=== :normal with a range runs on each line
ref:    various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   :1,2normal Ax<CR>
expect:
  onex
  two|x
  three
mode:   normal

=== :normal starts each line in the first column
ref:    various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Before executing the {commands}, the cursor is positioned in the first column of the range, for each line.
given:
  one tw|o
  three four
keys:   :%norm dw<CR>
expect:
  two
  |four
mode:   normal

=== :normal on the visual area
ref:    various.txt *:normal-range*
quote:  Execute Normal mode commands {commands} for each line in the {range}.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   Vj:norm I-<CR>
expect:
  -one
  |-two
  three
mode:   normal

=== :pu puts a register as new lines below
ref:    change.txt *:pu*
quote:  Put the text [from register x] after [line] (default current line).  This always works |linewise|
given:
  |one two
  three
keys:   yiw:pu<CR>
expect:
  one two
  |one
  three
mode:   normal

=== :pu! puts above
ref:    change.txt *:pu*
quote:  Put the text [from register x] before [line] (default current line).
given:
  one
  |two
keys:   yy:pu!<CR>
expect:
  one
  |two
  two
mode:   normal

=== :0pu puts above the first line
ref:    change.txt *:pu*
quote:  Put the text [from register x] after [line] (default current line).
given:
  one
  |two
keys:   yy:0pu<CR>
expect:
  |two
  one
  two
mode:   normal

=== :$pu x puts a named register at the end
ref:    change.txt *:pu*
quote:  Put the text [from register x] after [line] (default current line).
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   "ayy:$pu a<CR>
expect:
  one
  two
  |one
mode:   normal
